    "narrative": "The Austin Waves lineup faces a pivotal slate today, anchored by **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (71.15) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (69.06), who both benefit from favorable matchups against mid-rotation arms. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** is our premier start; he thrives against King\u2019s high-velocity profile, with a +14% boost from a dynamic platoon edge. Similarly, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** capitalizes on a high-efficiency matchup against Dobnak, whose 4.62 xERA provides the ideal environment for Vladdy to drive in runs. We are also leaning heavily into our leadoff speed, with **Sam Antonacci** (67.67) primed for a strong day against Ober; his +10% order boost and excellent platoon split make him a critical component for chasing the scarce stolen base category that defines our current roster strategy.\n\nThe decision to bench **Wade Meckler** (36.92) was the most difficult call of the morning, ultimately governed by our strict 40-point \"Zebras Floor.\" While **Wade Meckler** possesses the elite sprint speed we covet, the brutal matchup against Skenes\u2014who carries an elite 3.26 xERA\u2014effectively nullified his upside. Despite the boost from a #3 order slot, the sheer dominance of the opposing arm keeps him on the pine to preserve our limited game caps. Conversely, we are keeping a close watch on **Gunnar Henderson** (51.91); while he holds a respectable score, his production is hampered today by a negative platoon shift against Tolle, making him a candidate to underperform relative to his season-long expectations. We continue to monitor the status of **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Jacob Wilson** on the IL, but with **Drake Baldwin** and **Nasim Nunez** providing serviceable floor value at their respective positions, the core remains stable heading into first pitch.",
